---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'How Clipwell handles URLs, temporary media files, rate-limit data, server logs and contact emails. No accounts, no tracking cookies, no sold data.';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={description}
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what Clipwell processes when you use the website and downloader, why it is
    processed, and how long it is kept. It applies to the public Clipwell website and its downloader
    API. It does not apply to the platforms you link to; those services have their own privacy
    policies.
  </p>

  <p>
    Clipwell does not require an account. You can use the core downloader without giving a name,
    email address or payment detail. The service does, however, receive the media URL you submit and
    the technical information needed to process it safely.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we process</h2>

  <h3>Links and public media information</h3>

  <p>
    When you submit a URL, the backend receives the link and validates its hostname against a
    supported-platform allowlist. It then requests public page and media metadata from the platform,
    such as the title, uploader name, description, duration, thumbnail URL, available formats and
    caption tracks. This information is used to show the result and create the file you asked for.
  </p>

  <p>
    The application does not receive or store your platform password, session cookie or private
    account data. Do not submit links that contain sign-in tokens or other sensitive query
    parameters.
  </p>

  <h3>Technical and security data</h3>

  <p>
    The API uses your IP address to apply rate limits and prevent abuse. Rate-limit counters are held
    in memory for a short window and are not used to build a profile. Standard server logs may include
    the request time, route, response status, IP address and user agent. Those logs are used for
    security, debugging and capacity planning and are kept according to the hosting environment’s
    retention settings.
  </p>

  <h3>Temporary download files</h3>

  <p>
    Downloaded media, audio and caption files are written to a temporary directory on the downloader
    server. They are available through a job-specific link for a limited period and are removed
    automatically. The default retention window is approximately 15 minutes after a job completes,
    after which the link stops working. The extracted metadata record held in memory expires sooner
    or around the same time.
  </p>

  <p>
    Temporary files are not used to create a searchable library, train a model or serve other users.
    If the service is interrupted before cleanup runs, the operator’s normal host maintenance and
    restart procedures remove the temporary workspace.
  </p>

  <h3>Emails you send</h3>

  <p>
    If you contact support, privacy or legal addresses, we receive the email address you use, the
    content of your message and any attachments you choose to send. Do not send passwords, cookies or
    private media. Correspondence is kept only as long as needed to answer the request and meet legal
    obligations.
  </p>

  <h3>Local storage, not tracking cookies</h3>

  <p>
    The site stores your light or dark theme choice in your browser’s local storage under the key
    <code>clipwell-theme</code>. It is a preference, not an identifier, and it stays on your device.
    Clipwell does not set advertising cookies, use cross-site trackers, run analytics scripts or sell
    personal information. If a future deployment adds analytics, this policy and the site’s consent
    controls must be updated before it is enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we process it</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Provide the service:</strong> validate the link, fetch public metadata, produce the requested download and report progress.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep the service available:</strong> enforce request limits, prevent abuse, diagnose failures and manage temporary storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Protect rights and safety:</strong> respond to copyright complaints, legal requests and security incidents.</li>
    <li><strong>Comply with law:</strong> retain information where a valid legal obligation applies.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Where data protection law requires a legal basis, processing is based on the performance of the
    service you request, the operator’s legitimate interests in security and reliability, compliance
    with legal obligations, or consent where it is specifically obtained. You can object to
    processing based on legitimate interests using the privacy contact below.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing and third parties</h2>

  <p>
    A download request necessarily causes the backend to contact the platform whose URL you supplied.
    That platform receives the request and may see the backend’s IP address and standard request
    information, as it would for any visitor. Clipwell does not control the platform’s subsequent
    processing.
  </p>

  <p>
    We may use infrastructure providers for hosting, storage, security and email. They process data
    on the operator’s behalf under their own service terms. We may also disclose information if
    required by law, to protect the service or users, or in connection with a reorganisation. We do
    not sell personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Extraction records:</strong> held in memory briefly so a download job can refer to the selected format, then expired.</li>
    <li><strong>Download files:</strong> deleted automatically after the short job window, normally within 15 minutes.</li>
    <li><strong>Rate-limit counters:</strong> reset after the relevant short time window.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained for the short period configured by the hosting provider, unless needed for a specific security or legal investigation.</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> retained while the request is open and for a reasonable period afterwards for records and legal compliance.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>

  <p>
    Clipwell validates URLs before fetching, restricts the backend to supported platform domains,
    enforces request and file-size limits, runs processing commands without a shell, and removes
    temporary files. Production deployments should use HTTPS and keep credentials and environment
    configuration outside the public frontend. No internet service can promise absolute security, so
    do not submit sensitive personal data or credentials through the downloader.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to
    the processing of your personal data, or to receive a portable copy. You may also have the right
    to complain to your local data-protection authority. Because Clipwell does not maintain user
    accounts, we may need the approximate time of your request or another detail to locate any
    relevant log entry.
  </p>

  <p>
    Send privacy requests to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>. We may need to verify that a
    request relates to you before acting on it. Do not include identity documents unless we ask for
    them through a secure route.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>

  <p>
    The service may be hosted or supported in countries other than yours. Where required, the
    operator should use appropriate safeguards for international transfers, such as standard
    contractual clauses, and apply the same protections described in this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    Clipwell is a general-audience utility and is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum
    digital-consent age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal information from
    children. If you believe a child has sent personal information, contact us so it can be removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

  <p>
    This policy may be updated when the service, infrastructure or legal requirements change. The
    date at the top of the page shows the latest revision. Material changes should be communicated on
    the site before they take effect where practical.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Privacy questions and requests:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.privacyEmail}`}>{SITE.privacyEmail}</a>. General support:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. This policy is a transparency
    statement, not legal advice.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
